# SlabStack configuration. Copy to .env and edit as needed — every value has a
# working default, so an empty .env is fine.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# Put it in the repository root (this directory) or in backend/. Both are read,
# nearest last. It works the same however you start the app — `docker compose
# up`, `make api` and `make doctor` all see it — and anything already exported
# in your shell wins over the file.

# Where the SQLite database and uploaded images live. Back this directory up:
# it is your entire collection, price history and analysis.
# SLABSTACK_DATA_DIR=./backend/data

# Override the SQLAlchemy URL (defaults to sqlite at DATA_DIR/slabstack.db).
# SLABSTACK_DATABASE_URL=sqlite+pysqlite:////absolute/path/slabstack.db

# SLABSTACK_HOST=127.0.0.1
# SLABSTACK_PORT=8000

# Upload limit in bytes (default 25 MB).
# SLABSTACK_MAX_IMAGE_BYTES=26214400

# --- Market data providers ---------------------------------------------------
# Keys are read from the environment at call time. The database stores only the
# NAME of the variable, never a key. Setting one here does not switch a source
# on: that is a decision you take in Settings -> Data sources.

# The card catalogue. Works with no key at all; a key only raises the daily
# ceiling. This is the one source that ships switched on.
# SLABSTACK_POKEMONTCG_API_KEY=

# eBay. The only source that supplies individual sold listings, which is what
# liquidity, trend and — via graded comparables — the grading decision need.
# Both are required: create an application at developer.ebay.com, where the
# App ID is the client id and the Cert ID is the client secret.
#
# Sold listings additionally need Marketplace Insights, which eBay grants per
# application. Without it the source still works and records active listings;
# there are simply no sold prices until it is approved.
# SLABSTACK_EBAY_APP_ID=
# SLABSTACK_EBAY_CERT_ID=

# PriceCharting. Graded prices as named fields — the number the grade-or-sell
# decision turns on, and the only source here that supplies it without an
# approval process. Needs a paid subscription; there is no anonymous tier.
#
# It reuses video-game condition fields for card grades, so confirm the mapping
# before trusting it:  make pricecharting-fields CARD="Umbreon VMAX"
# SLABSTACK_PRICECHARTING_API_KEY=

# Listed, but no adapter is written for these yet.
# SLABSTACK_POKEPRICE_API_KEY=
# SLABSTACK_CARDMARKET_TOKEN=
# SLABSTACK_TCGPLAYER_TOKEN=
